WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:05.03
Part two ran every stage with a scripted stand-in.

00:00:05.03 --> 00:00:07.92
In part three, stage zero does real work.

00:00:07.92 --> 00:00:11.16
Hewn creates the product's private repository,

00:00:11.16 --> 00:00:16.45
then copies the Greenlit skills into it and records exactly what it copied,

00:00:16.45 --> 00:00:19.91
so every later stage can rely on the same skills.

00:00:21.06 --> 00:00:22.83
Two pieces share the job.

00:00:22.83 --> 00:00:28.42
When a worker first leases stage zero, the API creates the repository under the

00:00:28.42 --> 00:00:33.52
configured GitHub owner, named from the project in lowercase kebab case.

00:00:33.52 --> 00:00:39.11
Then the worker's bootstrap executor clones Greenlit, copies the skill folders,

00:00:39.11 --> 00:00:41.31
writes a lock file and commits.

00:00:41.66 --> 00:00:44.70
The worker never holds a GitHub credential.

00:00:44.70 --> 00:00:48.66
It reads and writes the repository only through the API,

00:00:48.66 --> 00:00:51.28
which checks the lease on every call.

00:00:52.43 --> 00:00:54.07
Creation is idempotent.

00:00:54.07 --> 00:00:59.59
If an earlier attempt created the repository but crashed before recording it,

00:00:59.59 --> 00:01:04.68
the API finds a fresh repository carrying the hewn topic and adopts it.

00:01:04.68 --> 00:01:09.12
A name taken by anything else fails the stage with the reason,

00:01:09.12 --> 00:01:11.26
and the project shows Blocked.

00:01:11.61 --> 00:01:17.12
The commit goes through a fenced mutation with an idempotency key made of the run

00:01:17.12 --> 00:01:18.00
and the step.

00:01:18.00 --> 00:01:23.51
A worker that resumes after a crash repeats the request and gets the first commit

00:01:23.51 --> 00:01:25.20
back, never a second one.

00:01:25.20 --> 00:01:30.91
Stage zero may write only the two skill folders and the lock file; any other path is

00:01:30.91 --> 00:01:31.45
refused.

00:01:32.60 --> 00:01:35.11
The bootstrap executor has two steps.

00:01:35.11 --> 00:01:38.78
The first clones the skills source named in the lease.

00:01:38.78 --> 00:01:42.71
The second asks the API which skill folders already exist,

00:01:42.71 --> 00:01:46.58
keeps those untouched and logs each one as kept existing,

00:01:46.58 --> 00:01:51.80
then commits everything else with the message Bootstrap skills from greenlit,

00:01:51.80 --> 00:01:53.43
at the short commit SHA.

00:01:53.78 --> 00:01:59.47
The lock file records the source, the full commit SHA and the names of the skills it

00:01:59.47 --> 00:01:59.95
copied.

00:01:59.95 --> 00:02:04.70
If Greenlit can't be reached, the run fails with Greenlit unreachable,

00:02:04.70 --> 00:02:05.85
and nothing more.

00:02:07.00 --> 00:02:12.93
The backend gained thirteen acceptance tests against an in-memory GitHub: creation,

00:02:12.93 --> 00:02:17.71
adoption, a taken name, the path rules, idempotency, a stale epoch,

00:02:17.71 --> 00:02:19.28
and redacted run logs.

00:02:19.28 --> 00:02:25.28
The worker gained six, against a real local git repository standing in for Greenlit.

00:02:25.28 --> 00:02:30.42
Playwright builds the same kind of fixture and runs stage zero for real.

00:02:31.57 --> 00:02:34.62
Here is the real app, with one worker running.

00:02:34.62 --> 00:02:37.27
The Owner names the project and submits.

00:02:37.27 --> 00:02:39.91
The page opens with every stage Pending.

00:02:39.91 --> 00:02:44.88
Moments later the worker leases stage zero, the API creates the repository,

00:02:44.88 --> 00:02:48.32
and its link appears in the header without a reload.

00:02:48.32 --> 00:02:53.74
Stage zero copies the skills and succeeds, and stage one starts straight after it.

00:02:53.74 --> 00:02:56.92
The remaining stages are still scripted for now.

00:02:57.27 --> 00:03:00.04
The link sits beside the direction on desktop,

00:03:00.04 --> 00:03:02.82
and wraps neatly on a phone in the dark theme.

00:03:03.97 --> 00:03:08.62
Stage zero now creates the repository and installs the skills,

00:03:08.62 --> 00:03:12.89
with no credential on the worker and no repeated commits.

00:03:12.89 --> 00:03:16.87
Next, the document stages: idea, stack, requirements,

00:03:16.87 --> 00:03:19.50
detailed designs and user journeys.
